---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Brady Ewing is documenting the path to design and build a Greendominium — a house inside a greenhouse. The examples here are credited inspiration."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The path</p>
      <h1>About Greendominium</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Brady Ewing is gathering the notes, stills, and questions that will shape a house
        inside a greenhouse of his own. This site is the public scrapbook.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Not a product line</h2>
      <p>
        Greendominium is a name for an idea: a livable core under glass, the barndominium
        of a greenhouse. The builds in the gallery were designed by other architects and
        made by other greenhouse shops. Each page names them.
      </p>
      <p>
        We show those homes because they already work. They are credited inspiration, not
        Greendominium inventory. Architect, greenhouse maker, other builders, and
        photographers are named on every profile — with links to their own sites when we have them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 1.2rem;">
      <h2>How the catalog stays small</h2>
      <p>
        Brady has almost no spare time. CoS maintains this site. A new example is a
        markdown file plus images — same fields every time, so the gallery stays scannable.
      </p>
      <p>
        Follow along on the <a href={site.facebookUrl}>{site.facebookLabel}</a> (placeholder
        until the page is live).
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/examples">See the examples</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
